            </connector>
            <label>More Than one Session</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>1. Remove concurrent sessions of the user who is currently logged in. As per the security requirement salesforce should only have one session at a time. So if a user logs in to a different browser or into other system the previous sessions are ended and user will be logged in with the current active session and will always have only one session for a user in salesforce.
2. Allow login only if user is using a supported browser.</description>
    <formulas>
        <name>Is_Browser_Supported</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>AND(
  NOT(CONTAINS({!LoginFlow_UserAgent},&quot;Edge&quot;)),
  OR(
    CONTAINS({!LoginFlow_UserAgent},&quot;Firefox&quot;),
    CONTAINS({!LoginFlow_UserAgent},&quot;Chrome&quot;),
    CONTAINS({!LoginFlow_UserAgent},&quot;Safari&quot;),
    CONTAINS({!LoginFlow_UserAgent},&quot;Edg&quot;)
  )
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Remove Concurrent Sessions {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Remove Concurrent Sessions</label>
